### End-to-end smoke test: composes requests from other files into one flow.
### Run this whole file with <leader>Ra to sanity-check the full user
### lifecycle in one shot — great for a quick "is the API alive" check
### before starting work, or in CI.

import ./auth/login.http
import ./users/create-user.http
import ./users/delete-user.http

### Step 1: log in (sets {{authToken}} globally for every request below)
run #LOGIN

### Step 2: create a user (also verifies it can be fetched right after)
run #CREATE_USER

### Step 3: clean up — delete the user we just made
# Note: delete-user.http currently deletes a hardcoded @userId — in a real
# suite you'd chain CREATE_USER's returned id into this instead, e.g.:
#   DELETE {{baseUrl}}/users/{{CREATE_USER.response.body.$.id}}
